.TH "UNCLOUD" 7 "March 2026" "atomdns handlers" "atomdns authors"

.SH "NAME"
.PP
\fIuncloud\fP \- power Uncloud dynamic registrations

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
The \fIuncloud\fP handler implements parts the web API of
uncloud\-dns
\[la]https://github.com/psviderski/uncloud-dns\[ra]. Uncloud only uses this to create names and records, so that
are the only handlers implemented.

.PP
It uses a SQLite database to persist these records. The database used is compatible with the \fIdbsqlite\fP
handler, and in fact to serve records from the database you must also enable the \fIdbsqlite\fP handler. The
\fIuncloud\fP handler assumes full ownership of the database and will purge old records (after 30 days), even if
they are not written by this handler.

.PP
If the global config contains a \fB\fCtls\fR section those certificates are used for the server, and a TLS server is
started.

.PP
The \fIuncloud\fP handler can only have a single zone, multiple zones will lead to an error.

.SH "SYNTAX"
.PP
.RS

.nf
uncloud DATABASE {
    addr ADDRESS
}

.fi
.RE

.IP \(bu 4
\fBDATABASE\fP the SQLite database to use. If the path is relative, the path from the global root path will be
prepended to it. This must be the same database as \fIdbsqlite\fP will use.
.IP \(bu 4
with \fB\fCaddr\fR you specify where the \fBADDRESS\fP of the server. It defaults to \fB\fC[::]:443\fR even without TLS.


.PP
If \fBDATABASE\fP does not exists and error is returned.

.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
Allow registrations and queries for \fB\fCuncloud.example.org\fR and \fB\fCuncl.example.net\fR.

.PP
.RS

.nf
uncld.example.org {
    dbsqlite uncl.db
    uncloud uncl.db
}

.fi
.RE

